    {
      "text": "have just men to be your kings, Mosiah 23:8. do your business by the voice of the people, Mosiah 29:26. Moroni took … the government of their wars, Alma 43:17. that they might maintain a free government, Alma 46:35. in a manner to overthrow the free government, Alma 51:5. rob them of their right to the government, Alma 54:17. to obtain their rights to the government, Alma 54:24. there is some faction in the government, Alma 58:36. Moroni was angry with the government, Alma 59:13. judgments of God … because of … slothfulness of our government, Alma 60:14. cleansed our inward vessel, yea, even the great head of our government, Alma 60:24. so much difficulty in the government, Hel. 1:18. governments were established by the voice of the people, Hel. 5:2. obtain the sole management of the government, Hel. 6:39. to be held in office at the head of government, Hel. 7:5. my people may recover their rights and government, 3 Ne. 3:10. they did destroy the government of the land, 3 Ne. 7:2. regulations of the government were destroyed, 3 Ne. 7:6. entered into a covenant to destroy the government, 3 Ne. 7:11. not united as to their laws, and their manner of government, 3 Ne. 7:14. did destroy the peace of my people and the government, 3 Ne. 9:9.",
